From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: debounce USB role changes

Every USB ID and USB source-detect interrupt schedules the detect work
20 ms out, and the work switches the DWC3 role at once. While a cable
goes in or out, the ID pin and VBUS bounce, so the controller is
switched between host and device mode faster than one switch can tear
down.

On a Redmi 4 Prime (msm8953-xiaomi-markw) this hung the SoC: the journal
of the frozen boot shows the xHCI host added, removed, the gadget bound
and the host added again within 1.6 s, then nothing. There was no oops;
the screen froze until a held power key reset the phone.

Restart a 500 ms timer on each interrupt instead, so the role follows
the cable only once it has settled. The delay still covers the 15 ms the
fuel gauge's ADC needs for the ID resistance. Log each role change, so
that the next hang shows which switch it was in.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@

 #include "qcom-smbchg.h"

+/*
+ * A plug or unplug makes the ID pin and VBUS bounce. Act on them only once
+ * they have been stable this long, so that DWC3 is not switched between
+ * host and device mode while a previous switch is still tearing down.
+ */
+#define SMBCHG_DETECT_DEBOUNCE_MS	500
+
 /**
  * find_closest_smaller - locate the closest smaller element in a sorted array
  * @x: The reference value.
@@ -957,6 +964,9 @@
 	}

 	if (usb_role != chip->last_role) {
+		dev_info(chip->dev, "USB role %s -> %s\n",
+			 usb_role_string(chip->last_role),
+			 usb_role_string(usb_role));
 		usb_role_switch_set_role(chip->role_sw, usb_role);
 		chip->last_role = usb_role;
 	}
@@ -1041,7 +1051,8 @@
 {
 	struct smbchg_chip *chip = data;

-	schedule_delayed_work(&chip->detect_work, msecs_to_jiffies(20));
+	mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &chip->detect_work,
+			 msecs_to_jiffies(SMBCHG_DETECT_DEBOUNCE_MS));
 	power_supply_changed(chip->usb_psy);

 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
@@ -1054,11 +1065,11 @@
 	/*
 	 * ADC conversion for USB ID resistance in the fuel gauge can take
 	 * up to 15ms to finish after the USB ID change interrupt is fired.
-	 * Wait for it to finish before detecting OTG presence. Add an extra
-	 * 5ms for good measure.
+	 * The debounce delay below covers it.
 	 */

-	schedule_delayed_work(&chip->detect_work, msecs_to_jiffies(20));
+	mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &chip->detect_work,
+			 msecs_to_jiffies(SMBCHG_DETECT_DEBOUNCE_MS));

 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
